                <a href="assets.html" class="active">Assets Guide</a>
                <a href="timeline.html">Timeline</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <div class="content">
        <div class="header">
            <h1>Campaign Assets Guide</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">How to create high-value assets for maximum impact</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Hub -->
        <div class="asset-card">
            <div class="asset-header">
                <div class="asset-icon">🏠</div>
                <div class="asset-title">
                    <h2>Content Hub</h2>
                    <p class="asset-type">Evergreen Resource Center</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>What It Is</h3>
                <p>A comprehensive, SEO-optimized landing page that serves as the central resource for a specific topic (e.g., "How to Launch a Private Practice"). It aggregates blog posts, guides, tools, and other resources into one navigable destination.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>How to Make It Valuable</h3>
                <div class="tips-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Comprehensive structure:</strong> Cover all major subtopics with clear navigation</li>
                        <li><strong>Internal linking:</strong> Connect to relevant blog posts, guides, and campaign assets</li>
                        <li><strong>Progressive depth:</strong> Start with overview content, link to deeper dives</li>
                        <li><strong>Regular updates:</strong> Keep content current with latest regulations, trends, data</li>
                        <li><strong>Clear CTAs:</strong> Guide visitors to campaign assets (course, checklist) at natural points</li>
                        <li><strong>Visual hierarchy:</strong> Use headers, cards, and sections for easy scanning</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="best-practice">
                <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Design the hub to answer common questions at different stages of the journey. Each section should link to either a blog post (for awareness) or a campaign asset (for conversion).
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Course/Interactive Checklist -->
        <div class="asset-card">
            <div class="asset-header">
                <div class="asset-icon">🎓</div>
                <div class="asset-title">
                    <h2>Course / Interactive Checklist</h2>
                    <p class="asset-type">Lead Magnet & Conversion Asset</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>What It Is</h3>
                <p>A structured, actionable resource that guides users through a specific process (e.g., CQC registration). Can be a multi-module course, an interactive checklist with guidance, or a combination of both.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>How to Make It Valuable</h3>
                <div class="tips-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Modular structure:</strong> Break into digestible steps (5-7 modules ideal)</li>
                        <li><strong>Actionable content:</strong> Every section should have clear next steps</li>
                        <li><strong>Templates included:</strong> Provide downloadable documents, checklists, worksheets</li>
                        <li><strong>Progress tracking:</strong> Show users how far they've come and what's left</li>
                        <li><strong>Expert credibility:</strong> Feature insights from Jonathan or other experts</li>
                        <li><strong>Mixed media:</strong> Combine text, video, downloadables for different learning styles</li>
                        <li><strong>Community element:</strong> If using Circle.so, enable peer discussion</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="best-practice">
                <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Start with text-based modules for speed, then add video and interactivity over time. Each module should end with a clear "what to do next" action.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Video Content -->
        <div class="asset-card">
            <div class="asset-header">
                <div class="asset-icon">🎥</div>
                <div class="asset-title">
                    <h2>Video Content</h2>
                    <p class="asset-type">Multi-Purpose Promotional Asset</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>What It Is</h3>
                <p>Short-form (2-5 min) or long-form (10-15 min) video content featuring Jonathan or experts explaining key concepts, common pitfalls, or success stories related to private practice launch.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>How to Make It Valuable</h3>
                <div class="tips-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Modular shooting:</strong> Film multiple topics in one session for efficiency</li>
                        <li><strong>Repurpose-first mindset:</strong> Structure for easy cutting into shorter clips</li>
                        <li><strong>Strong hooks:</strong> First 3-5 seconds must grab attention for social</li>
                        <li><strong>Subtitles always:</strong> Essential for social media consumption</li>
                        <li><strong>Multiple formats:</strong> Horizontal (YouTube), square (LinkedIn/FB), vertical (Stories/Shorts)</li>
                        <li><strong>CTA at end:</strong> Direct viewers to hub or course enrollment</li>
                        <li><strong>B-roll and graphics:</strong> Keep visually engaging, avoid talking heads only</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="best-practice">
                <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Create video with three uses in mind: 1) embedded in course/hub, 2) ads on social, 3) organic social posts. Script and shoot accordingly.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Blog Content -->
        <div class="asset-card">
            <div class="asset-header">
                <div class="asset-icon">📝</div>
                <div class="asset-title">
                    <h2>Blog Content</h2>
                    <p class="asset-type">SEO & Awareness Driver</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>What It Is</h3>
                <p>SEO-optimized articles (800-1500 words) addressing specific questions or pain points related to launching a private practice. Serves as top-of-funnel content to drive organic traffic.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>How to Make It Valuable</h3>
                <div class="tips-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Keyword research:</strong> Target long-tail queries with clear search intent</li>
                        <li><strong>Answer-first format:</strong> Get to the point quickly, expand with detail</li>
                        <li><strong>Internal linking:</strong> Link to hub and related blog posts (3-5 internal links minimum)</li>
                        <li><strong>Clear CTA:</strong> At end, direct to course/checklist or hub for "next steps"</li>
                        <li><strong>Expert quotes:</strong> Include Jonathan's insights for credibility</li>
                        <li><strong>Scannable format:</strong> Use headers, bullets, short paragraphs</li>
                        <li><strong>Regular publishing:</strong> Consistency matters for SEO (2-4 posts/month)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="best-practice">
                <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Write blogs with hub structure in mind. Each blog should naturally fit into a hub category and link back to it. Think of blogs as "spokes" feeding the "hub."
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Webinar -->
        <div class="asset-card">
            <div class="asset-header">
                <div class="asset-icon">💻</div>
                <div class="asset-title">
                    <h2>Webinar</h2>
                    <p class="asset-type">Live Engagement & Lead Generation</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>What It Is</h3>
                <p>A live or pre-recorded 30-45 minute session with Jonathan (or expert) covering a high-value topic, with time for Q&A. Used as a launch event or ongoing engagement tool.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>How to Make It Valuable</h3>
                <div class="tips-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Clear value prop:</strong> Promote specific takeaways attendees will get</li>
                        <li><strong>Timed with launch:</strong> Schedule around course/checklist availability</li>
                        <li><strong>Interactive elements:</strong> Polls, Q&A, chat to boost engagement</li>
                        <li><strong>Slide deck:</strong> Share as downloadable resource post-webinar</li>
                        <li><strong>Recording strategy:</strong> Offer replay to registrants who miss it</li>
                        <li><strong>Follow-up sequence:</strong> Email attendees with course offer within 24 hours</li>
                        <li><strong>Repurpose content:</strong> Cut into short clips for social and ads</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="best-practice">
                <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Structure as 60% teaching, 20% Q&A, 20% soft pitch for course. Make the teaching so valuable that the course becomes a natural next step.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Case Studies -->
        <div class="asset-card">
            <div class="asset-header">
                <div class="asset-icon">📊</div>
                <div class="asset-title">
                    <h2>Case Studies</h2>
                    <p class="asset-type">Social Proof & Credibility</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>What It Is</h3>
                <p>Real customer success stories showing how Semble customers launched their practices. Can be written, video interviews, or mixed media.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>How to Make It Valuable</h3>
                <div class="tips-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Problem-Solution-Result format:</strong> Clear narrative arc</li>
                        <li><strong>Specific metrics:</strong> Time saved, patients seen, revenue impact</li>
                        <li><strong>Quote-heavy:</strong> Let customer voice come through authentically</li>
                        <li><strong>Visual elements:</strong> Photos of practice, screenshots of Semble in action</li>
                        <li><strong>Multiple formats:</strong> Long-form written + short video testimonial</li>
                        <li><strong>Hub integration:</strong> Feature case studies prominently on relevant hub sections</li>
                        <li><strong>Specialty diversity:</strong> Show different practice types (GP, dental, aesthetics)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="best-practice">
                <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Focus case studies on the transformation journey, not just Semble features. Show how they went from "stuck at registration" to "thriving practice."
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Social Content -->
        <div class="asset-card">
            <div class="asset-header">
                <div class="asset-icon">📱</div>
                <div class="asset-title">
                    <h2>Social Content</h2>
                    <p class="asset-type">Organic Reach & Community Building</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>What It Is</h3>
                <p>Short-form posts, carousels, video clips, and stories shared on LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook promoting hub content, blog posts, and campaign assets.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>How to Make It Valuable</h3>
                <div class="tips-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Snippet strategy:</strong> Pull key insights from blogs/videos as standalone posts</li>
                        <li><strong>Carousel posts:</strong> Turn blog sections into visual carousels (LinkedIn loves these)</li>
                        <li><strong>Question posts:</strong> Ask community questions, link to hub for answers</li>
                        <li><strong>Behind-the-scenes:</strong> Show Jonathan filming, course creation, customer wins</li>
                        <li><strong>Consistent posting:</strong> 3-5x/week to maintain visibility</li>
                        <li><strong>Engagement focus:</strong> Comment on related posts, build community</li>
                        <li><strong>Always link back:</strong> Every post should drive to hub, blog, or course</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="best-practice">
                <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Create social content in batches by repurposing existing assets. One blog post = 5-7 social posts. One video = 10+ clips/quotes.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Email Sequences -->
        <div class="asset-card">
            <div class="asset-header">
                <div class="asset-icon">📧</div>
                <div class="asset-title">
                    <h2>Email Sequences</h2>
                    <p class="asset-type">Nurture & Conversion Driver</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>What It Is</h3>
                <p>Automated email sequences triggered by course enrollment, webinar attendance, or hub downloads. Guides leads through their journey with valuable content and soft CTAs.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="asset-section">
                <h3>How to Make It Valuable</h3>
                <div class="tips-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Welcome series:</strong> 3-5 emails introducing course, setting expectations</li>
                        <li><strong>Progress nudges:</strong> Remind users to complete modules with specific value props</li>
                        <li><strong>Value-first approach:</strong> Each email teaches something, not just promotes</li>
                        <li><strong>Segmentation:</strong> Different sequences for course completers vs. non-starters</li>
                        <li><strong>Clear CTAs:</strong> One primary action per email</li>
                        <li><strong>Timing optimization:</strong> Test send times for engagement</li>
                        <li><strong>Re-engagement campaigns:</strong> Win back inactive course enrollees</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="best-practice">
                <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Map email sequences to user behavior. If they complete Module 1, congratulate and tease Module 2. If they stall, send case study showing ROI of completion.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

:::
